# Boot from a save and load it (port/test/README.md, "Chapter saves").
# Play with GATE0_SRAM_IN set to the save. Each press comes in a state that
# waits for input, at least 150 ticks after that state began on the GBA, so
# the lag-free PC takes the same path. Checked on the GBA with the two saves
# of the chapsave presets: the save is loaded at tick 1,735.
#
# The title menu opens on its first entry: "Resume Chapter" when the save has
# a valid suspend, otherwise "Restart Chapter" (Continue), and the slot list
# then opens on the last saved slot (port/test/tools/sram_info.py tells which).
#
# 2,000 entries (ticks 0-1,999): append keys from tick 2,000.
000*250
001*2      # 250: A, the health and safety screen (waiting for a key)
000*748
008*2      # 1000: Start, skips the opening to the title screen
000*298
001*2      # 1300: A, title screen: the title menu
000*198
001*2      # 1500: A, the first entry (Resume Chapter or Restart Chapter): the slot list
000*198
001*2      # 1700: A, load the slot (the game runs from tick 1,735)
000*298
# c10 shard C: from tick 2,000 (turn 1, cursor on a unit at (12,13)): Right to (13,13), A (map menu),
# Up (wraps to End), A (End): the enemy phase, where the Demon King summons on turn 1.
000*20
010*2      # 2020: Right
000*30
001*2      # 2052: A, the map menu
000*30
040*2      # 2084: Up, to End
000*20
001*2      # 2106: A, End
000*2892
